# Security Rules

## Never Do These

- NEVER store secrets, API keys, or tokens in code — use `process.env`
- NEVER use `eval()` or `Function()` constructor
- NEVER use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization
- NEVER log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, personal data)
- NEVER return stack traces or internal error details to clients
- NEVER skip input validation on any endpoint
- NEVER create a route without authentication unless explicitly public
- NEVER use `SELECT *` equivalent — always specify fields needed
- NEVER concatenate user input into queries

## Always Do These

- ALWAYS wrap async route handlers in asyncHandler or try-catch
- ALWAYS validate and sanitize all incoming data
- ALWAYS use parameterized queries
- ALWAYS return generic error messages to clients
- ALWAYS log errors server-side with winston
- ALWAYS check user authorization before data access
- ALWAYS use HTTPS-only cookies for sensitive tokens
- ALWAYS add rate limiting to new routes

## Input Validation Pattern

```javascript
const validators = [
  body('email').isEmail().normalizeEmail(),
  body('name').isString().trim().isLength({ min: 2, max: 100 }),
];
```

## Error Response Pattern

```javascript
// Wrong:
res.status(500).json({ error: err.message, stack: err.stack });

// Right:
res.status(500).json({ success: false, message: 'An error occurred. Please try again.' });
```
